{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**1. Contradictions**\n- #10 resume/cancel read status files and signal a detached supervisor; code uses in-memory `JobRegistry`/`cursor_cancel` child kill. → **#7 file + supervisor path**\n- #10 resume on any terminal status; `answer_delegation` only `NEEDS_CONTEXT`. → **file resume, any terminal**\n- `status_record_path` uses `cursor-delegate-jobs`; #4/#7 use `delegate-jobs`. → **rename with #7**\n- Disk writes bare `PollResult`; #7 needs `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt`, `resume {…}`. → **#7 record extensions**\n- `ResumeContext` keeps MCP fields (`isolation`, `verifyCommands`, `allowPartialCommit`); #4 resume stash is slimmer. → **store spec fields only**\n- `Capability`/`capability.rs` still Plan/Write; #4 is `read-only`/`read-write`. → **CLI names + mapping**\n- Cross-backend rejection implied via model table; code uses `family` in `resolve_model`. → **compare `backend` on entries**\n- Multi-backend session resume (#4 pi/claude flags) vs `build_argv` cursor `--resume` only. → **per-backend resume builder**\n\n**2. #10 unstated defaults**\n- Resume stdout (new id only vs JSON). → **match `run` (id line)**\n- Unknown/missing job exit code. → **exit 2, stderr reason**\n- Cancel on already-terminal job. → **exit 0, print record**\n- Signal for cancel. → **SIGTERM to supervisor process group**\n- Old job `supersededBy` after resume. → **set like MCP `mark_superseded`**\n\n**3. Unspecified failures**\n- Corrupt record JSON. → **exit 2 parse error**\n- Resume while `RUNNING`. → **exit 2**\n- Terminal record missing `sessionId`. → **exit 2 cannot resume**\n- Empty resume prompt. → **exit 2 (same as run)**\n- RW resume with cwd lock held (#4 BUSY). → **BUSY + holder id**\n\n**4. Acceptance vs spec/code**\n- E2E only MCP cancel, not CLI pg-kill. → **add `delegate` CLI e2e**\n- “Supervisor gone” for resume vs cancel needing live pid. → **resume yes; cancel only when RUNNING**\n- “Kill every process agent started” vs killing backend CLI. → **process-group kill suffices**\n- AC “original settings” vs overrides. → **overrides win (already stated)**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS"}]},"session_id":"9fe30b80-d334-4ff0-ad00-19ff619b32c9"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":40410,"duration_api_ms":40410,"is_error":false,"result":"Gathering issues #10, #4, #7 and the referenced source files for the preflight.\n\n\n**1. Contradictions**\n- #10 resume/cancel read status files and signal a detached supervisor; code uses in-memory `JobRegistry`/`cursor_cancel` child kill. → **#7 file + supervisor path**\n- #10 resume on any terminal status; `answer_delegation` only `NEEDS_CONTEXT`. → **file resume, any terminal**\n- `status_record_path` uses `cursor-delegate-jobs`; #4/#7 use `delegate-jobs`. → **rename with #7**\n- Disk writes bare `PollResult`; #7 needs `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt`, `resume {…}`. → **#7 record extensions**\n- `ResumeContext` keeps MCP fields (`isolation`, `verifyCommands`, `allowPartialCommit`); #4 resume stash is slimmer. → **store spec fields only**\n- `Capability`/`capability.rs` still Plan/Write; #4 is `read-only`/`read-write`. → **CLI names + mapping**\n- Cross-backend rejection implied via model table; code uses `family` in `resolve_model`. → **compare `backend` on entries**\n- Multi-backend session resume (#4 pi/claude flags) vs `build_argv` cursor `--resume` only. → **per-backend resume builder**\n\n**2. #10 unstated defaults**\n- Resume stdout (new id only vs JSON). → **match `run` (id line)**\n- Unknown/missing job exit code. → **exit 2, stderr reason**\n- Cancel on already-terminal job. → **exit 0, print record**\n- Signal for cancel. → **SIGTERM to supervisor process group**\n- Old job `supersededBy` after resume. → **set like MCP `mark_superseded`**\n\n**3. Unspecified failures**\n- Corrupt record JSON. → **exit 2 parse error**\n- Resume while `RUNNING`. → **exit 2**\n- Terminal record missing `sessionId`. → **exit 2 cannot resume**\n- Empty resume prompt. → **exit 2 (same as run)**\n- RW resume with cwd lock held (#4 BUSY). → **BUSY + holder id**\n\n**4. Acceptance vs spec/code**\n- E2E only MCP cancel, not CLI pg-kill. → **add `delegate` CLI e2e**\n- “Supervisor gone” for resume vs cancel needing live pid. → **resume yes; cancel only when RUNNING**\n- “Kill every process agent started” vs killing backend CLI. → **process-group kill suffices**\n- AC “original settings” vs overrides. → **overrides win (already stated)**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS","session_id":"9fe30b80-d334-4ff0-ad00-19ff619b32c9","request_id":"46fec545-9cff-4ca8-a876-d8b6b8772553","usage":{"inputTokens":40743,"outputTokens":3739,"cacheReadTokens":94652,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
